        <headline>High Wind Watch issued September 24 at 4:10PM EDT until September 26 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Wind Advisory, northeast winds 25 to 35 mph with
gusts up to 45 mph. For the High Wind Watch, north winds 30 to 40
mph with gusts up to 60 mph possible.

* WHERE...In Delaware, Delaware Beaches County. In New Jersey,
Eastern Monmouth, Atlantic Coastal Cape May, Coastal Atlantic, and
Coastal Ocean Counties.

* WHEN...For the Wind Advisory, until 6 PM EDT Friday. For the High
Wind Watch, from Friday evening through Saturday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds could blow down trees and power lines.
Widespread power outages are possible. Travel could be difficult,
especially for high profile vehicles. Gusty winds will blow around
unsecured objects. Tree limbs could be blown down and a few power
outages may result.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the latest forecasts and warnings for updates.

Fasten loose objects or shelter objects in a safe location prior to
the onset of winds.

Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.

Secure outdoor objects.</instruction>
